window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b24c4cceb411a4bf"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"developer-settings\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">开发者设置</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本的文档。</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex 的 IDE（集成开发环境）扩展有两层设置：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Codex 设置（Codex settings）</strong>控制与 Codex CLI 共用的智能体行为，包括模型、推理强度、权限、沙箱、MCP 服务器和个性化设置。Codex 从 <code>config.toml</code> 读取这些设置。</li> <li><strong>编辑器设置（Editor settings）</strong>控制扩展在 VS Code 及兼容编辑器中的行为。这些设置使用编辑器设置系统中的 <code>chatgpt.*</code> 键。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"open-codex-settings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">打开 Codex 设置</h2> <p>在 Codex 侧边栏中选择齿轮图标，然后选择 <strong>Codex Settings（Codex 设置）</strong>。常用的智能体控制项可在设置面板中调整；若要直接编辑当前生效的配置层，请选择 <strong>Open config.toml（打开 config.toml）</strong>。</p> <p>有关配置层的顺序和常用键，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>。有关所有受支持的 <code>config.toml</code> 键，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"change-an-editor-setting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">更改编辑器设置</h2> <p>若要更改设置，请按以下步骤操作：</p> <ol> <li>打开编辑器设置。</li> <li>搜索 <code>@ext:openai.chatgpt</code>、<code>Codex</code> 或设置名称。</li> <li>更新对应的值。</li> </ol> <p>此扩展也会采用 VS Code 内置的聊天字体设置，这些设置会应用于 Codex 聊天界面。</p> <p><a id=\"editor-settings-reference\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">编辑器设置参考</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>设置</th> <th>默认值</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.commentCodeLensEnabled</code></td> <td><code>true</code></td> <td>在 <code>TODO</code> 注释上方显示 CodeLens（代码行上方的提示信息），让 Codex 可以处理这些待办事项。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openOnStartup</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>扩展完成启动后，将焦点切换到 Codex 侧边栏。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.followUpQueueMode</code></td> <td><code>queue</code></td> <td>选择在任务运行期间发送的消息是等待下一次运行（<code>queue</code>），还是引导当前运行（<code>steer</code>）。对于旧版值 <code>interrupt</code>，扩展会按 <code>steer</code> 处理。按 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> 可针对单条消息反转此行为。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.composerEnterBehavior</code></td> <td><code>enter</code></td> <td>选择按 <kbd>Enter</kbd> 是否总是发送（<code>enter</code>）、按 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> 才发送多行提示（<code>cmdIfMultiline</code>），或始终必须使用修饰键（<code>cmdAlways</code>）。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.reviewDelivery</code></td> <td><code>inline</code></td> <td>尽可能在当前聊天中运行 <code>/review</code>（<code>inline</code>），或另开一个审查聊天（<code>detached</code>）。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.localeOverride</code></td> <td>Auto（自动）</td> <td>设置 Codex 界面首选语言。留空时会自动检测。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.runCodexInWindowsSubsystemForLinux</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>仅限 Windows：当 WSL 可用时，在 WSL 中运行 Codex。若代码仓库和工具位于 WSL2，或需要 Linux 原生工具，可使用此选项。更改此设置会重新加载 VS Code。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.cliExecutable</code></td> <td>Unset（未设置）</td> <td>仅用于开发：设置 Codex CLI 可执行文件的路径。除非你正在开发 Codex CLI，否则无需设置。手动覆盖随扩展捆绑的可执行文件，可能导致部分功能无法正常工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default（编辑器默认值）</td> <td>控制 Codex 侧边栏中的聊天文字，包括聊天内容和输入框。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.editor.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default（编辑器默认值）</td> <td>控制 Codex 聊天中以代码形式呈现的内容，包括代码片段和差异。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>上面的 <code>chatgpt.*</code> 键属于 IDE 扩展，不应写入 <code>config.toml</code>。如需配置智能体共用设置，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">高级配置</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"developer-settings\">Developer settings</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>The Codex IDE extension has two settings layers:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Codex settings</strong> control agent behavior shared with Codex CLI, including the model, reasoning effort, permissions, sandbox, MCP servers, and personalization. Codex reads these settings from <code>config.toml</code>.</li> <li><strong>Editor settings</strong> control how the extension behaves inside VS Code and compatible editors. These settings use <code>chatgpt.*</code> keys in the editor's settings system.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"open-codex-settings\">Open Codex settings</h2> <p>Select the gear icon in the Codex sidebar, then select <strong>Codex Settings</strong>. Use the settings panel for common agent controls, or select <strong>Open config.toml</strong> to edit the active configuration layer directly.</p> <p>For the configuration layer order and common keys, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>. For every supported <code>config.toml</code> key, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration reference</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"change-an-editor-setting\">Change an editor setting</h2> <p>To change a setting, follow these steps:</p> <ol> <li>Open your editor settings.</li> <li>Search for <code>@ext:openai.chatgpt</code>, <code>Codex</code>, or the setting name.</li> <li>Update the value.</li> </ol> <p>The extension also honors VS Code's built-in chat font settings for Codex chat surfaces.</p> <h2 id=\"editor-settings-reference\">Editor settings reference</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Setting</th> <th>Default</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.commentCodeLensEnabled</code></td> <td><code>true</code></td> <td>Show CodeLens above <code>TODO</code> comments so Codex can address them.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openOnStartup</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>Focus the Codex sidebar when the extension finishes starting.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.followUpQueueMode</code></td> <td><code>queue</code></td> <td>Choose whether messages sent during a run wait for the next run (<code>queue</code>) or steer the current run (<code>steer</code>). The extension treats the legacy <code>interrupt</code> value as <code>steer</code>. Press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> to invert the behavior for one message.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.composerEnterBehavior</code></td> <td><code>enter</code></td> <td>Choose whether <kbd>Enter</kbd> always sends (<code>enter</code>), <kbd>Cmd</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> sends multiline prompts (<code>cmdIfMultiline</code>), or the modifier is always required (<code>cmdAlways</code>).</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.reviewDelivery</code></td> <td><code>inline</code></td> <td>Run <code>/review</code> in the current chat when possible (<code>inline</code>) or start a separate review chat (<code>detached</code>).</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.localeOverride</code></td> <td>Auto</td> <td>Set the preferred language for the Codex UI. Leave empty to detect it automatically.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.runCodexInWindowsSubsystemForLinux</code></td> <td><code>false</code></td> <td>Windows only: Run Codex in WSL when WSL is available. Use this when your repositories and tooling live in WSL2 or when you need Linux-native tooling. Changing this setting reloads VS Code.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.cliExecutable</code></td> <td>Unset</td> <td>Development only: Set the path to the Codex CLI executable. You don't need this setting unless you're developing the Codex CLI; manually overriding the bundled executable can prevent parts of the extension from working.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default</td> <td>Control chat text in the Codex sidebar, including chat content and the composer.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chat.editor.fontSize</code></td> <td>Editor default</td> <td>Control code-rendered content in Codex chats, including code snippets and diffs.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The <code>chatgpt.*</code> keys above belong to the IDE extension and don't go in <code>config.toml</code>. For shared agent settings, use <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">Advanced configuration</a>, and the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration reference</a>.</p>"};
